## Key Analytical Flags

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>EoM ratio dual-basis discrepancy:</strong> The filing explicitly states an EOM ratio of <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">39%</span> (YTD, gross-direct-premium basis, Note 5) — used above — but also tabulates a separate "Expense of Management to Net Written Premium Ratio" of <strong>51.31%</strong> (Note 11, NWP-denominator basis). Both figures are statutory and correctly disclosed; they differ solely by denominator, not methodology error.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Profitability inflection within 9M:</strong> Q3 FY25 standalone PAT (<strong>₹13.24 cr</strong>) alone <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">exceeded</span> the entire 9M cumulative PAT of <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">₹7.44 cr</span>, implying H1 FY25 was roughly a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▼ ₹(5.80) cr net loss</span> on a standalone basis. This is consistent with one-time IPO-related expenses and a cumulative <strong>₹198.37 cr</strong> Excess-EOM transfer from revenue to P&L (Note 5) that depressed H1 profitability ahead of the November 14, 2024 listing.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Investment yield — favorable trend:</strong> Yield without unrealized gains <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▲ improved to 5.27%</span> in 9M FY25 vs. 4.81% in 9M FY24. However, yield <em>with</em> unrealized gains fell sharply in Q3 alone (<span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▼ 1.70%</span> vs. 2.92% in Q2), signaling mark-to-market volatility in the investment book that the core yield figure masks.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>GST/DGGI contingent liability (Note 7):</strong> The filing discloses a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">₹25 cr</span> payment made under Section 74(5) CGST Act, plus a pending Show Cause Notice covering <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">₹29.29 cr</span> of marketing expenses — a live, unresolved regulatory/tax exposure not reflected in the reported PAT.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Net worth figure reconciliation:</strong> "Net worth as at Dec 31, 2024" appears under both the three-months and YTD column headers with a minor ₹300 lakh discrepancy (₹2,86,584 lakh vs. ₹2,86,884 lakh) — likely a table-extraction artifact since both reference the identical balance-sheet date. The YTD-column figure (₹2,86,884 lakh = <strong>₹2868.84 cr</strong>) is reported per task instruction to prioritize the YTD column.
</div>

## Data Completeness Caveat

<div style="background:#EFF6FF;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;margin-bottom:6px;">Informational</div>

Several requested metrics — <strong>Retail health GWP, Retail health market share, AUM, Solvency ratio, and the standalone Claims/Expense/Commission/Combined ratios</strong> — are typically disclosed in a company's dedicated **"Investor Presentation 9MFY25"** deck rather than the statutory NL filing. That deck was **not among the five URLs specified** in the query and could not be located within the investor-relations index page reviewed (Doc #5). Per the "no-estimate" rule, these cells are left blank rather than back-calculated or approximated.

**Recommendation:** To complete the ratio and AUM/market-share fields, source Niva Bupa's standalone **"Investor Presentation — Q3 & 9M FY25"** PDF directly from the investor-relations financial-results archive (separate from the NL statutory disclosure), or the Q3 FY25 press release, both of which typically carry the headline combined/claims/expense ratios and Solvency ratio on an IGAAP basis.</ans>
